+# Inspector-general peer-review schedules and the missing 2006 DOT review
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review UTC · B129 / PD04–PD05, supporting PD02–PD03. The PCIE/ECIE **FY 2007 progress report** gives aggregate investigative-review counts and identifies the working group that updated the guide. An official agency-group schedule supplies a later, verifiable example of matching a planned reviewer to an actual DOT-reported release. These records identify where to look for the 2006 reviewer assignment, guide version and original transmittal. The **December 2006 EPA-on-DOT review**, its distribution and any connection to the FAA case remain unverified. [FY 2007 report, physical p. 24](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/fy07apr.pdf#page=24) · [Medium-agency schedule](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/oipeergrp_b.pdf)
+
+## Period guide and reporting records
+
+| Record and locator | What it documents |
+| --- | --- |
+| **FY 2006 PCIE/ECIE progress report**, printed p. 7, physical p. 13, lines 48–73 | Reports that the **Investigations Committee** revised the **Investigation Peer Review Guide**. The selected passage describes the purpose of the guide. It supplies no release date, copy or 2006 review-specific version. [Report](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/fy06apr.pdf#page=13) |
+| **FY 2007 PCIE/ECIE progress report**, printed p. 19, physical p. 24, lines 8–35, and physical p. 29, lines 16–24 | Reports **six OIGs** received a favorable investigative peer-review rating and **two** investigative reviews were in process at fiscal year end. The adjacent **17 PCIE and 9 ECIE** figures concern **audit** reviews underway or performed. The six and two are aggregate counts. The passage provides no agency-level roster to link the December 2006 EPA review to either group. The report separately says the assistant inspectors general for investigations working under the PCIE Investigations Committee updated peer-review guidelines in FY 2007. [Counts](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/fy07apr.pdf#page=24) · [Working group](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/fy07apr.pdf#page=29) |
+| **FY 2008 progress report**, printed p. 11, physical p. 17, lines 7–16 and 51–59 | Attributes a schedule through **2014** and a project to update the guide to the **Investigations Committee**. The separate **2009–2010** schedule and update on that page belong to the **Audit Committee**. Preserve the separate bodies and periods. The 2008 law established CIGIE and sets a transition for the earlier councils' executive orders. The statute and reports leave actual transfer of predecessor working records to be verified. [FY 2008 table](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/fy08apr.pdf#page=17) · [Transition provision](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/PLAW-110publ409/pdf/PLAW-110publ409.pdf#page=13) |
+
+The FY 2006 **revised** description, FY 2007 working-group **updated** description and FY 2008 **project to update** description are retained separately. Approval dates, draft histories and distribution copies are required to determine which changes applied to the EPA review. The existing PCIE and CIGIE attributions in DOT's budget editions remain side by side.
+
+## A tested schedule-to-outcome join
+
+- The three group schedules distinguish **reviewed office** and **reviewing office**. The medium and large sheets are dated **March 2011**, the small sheet **April 2012**. The small sheet is headed **Fiscal Years 2010–2014** and carries a **2009 (Feb-Mar-Apr 09)** entry. It also preserves a reviewer replacement, **Federal Reserve Board (replaced Commerce)**, in a separate 2012 row. The title, dates and replacement remain as shown. These documents demonstrate the assignment fields and the possibility of schedule revision. The underlying change records and the relationship of the sheets to the exact FY 2008 schedule remain unverified. [Small group](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/oipeergrp_a.pdf) · [Medium group](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/oipeergrp_b.pdf) · [Large group](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/oipeergrp_c.pdf)
+- The medium sheet's sorted text line **18** gives **Transportation** as reviewed office, **Treasury** as reviewing office and **May-Jun-Jul 12** as scheduled quarter. DOT's September 2012 semiannual report records Treasury as reviewer of DOT's **Office of Investigations**, reports compliance and no recommendations, and gives **August 30, 2012** as release date. Two 2013 DOT semiannual reports repeat that date. The scheduled quarter and reported release are distinct fields. The underlying engagement, actual fieldwork dates, report and recipient receipts remain missing. The historical DOT index cited by the 2012 report now returned HTTP **404** in this run. [September 2012, printed p. 111, physical p. 119](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/DOT-OIG%20Semiannual%20Report%20to%20Congress%5EApril%201%2C%202012%20-%20September%2030%2C%202012.PDF#page=119) · [March 2013, physical p. 121](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/OIG%20Semiannual%20Report%5EOctober%202012%20-%20March%202013.pdf#page=121) · [September 2013, physical p. 117](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/DOT%20OIG%20Semiannual%20Report%20to%20Congress%20-%20April-September%202013.pdf#page=117)
+- Preserve the direction of other rows. Medium line **9** lists **EPA as reviewed** and **Transportation as reviewer** for **Nov-Dec-Jan 11**, the reverse of the roles described for the December 2006 review. Medium line **19** lists **Veterans Affairs as reviewed** and **EPA as reviewer** for **Aug-Sep-Oct 12**. EPA's September 2013 report states it issued the VA investigative review on **August 23, 2013**, covering **October 1, 2011–September 30, 2012**. Keep schedule, covered period and issue date separate. This comparison supplies no evidence that any other scheduled row proceeded as planned. [Medium group, physical p. 1](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/oipeergrp_b.pdf) · [EPA report, printed p. 71, physical p. 76](https://nepis.epa.gov/Exe/ZyPDF.cgi?Dockey=P100H9K1.PDF#page=76)
+
+## Scope and remaining records
+
+Eleven official PDFs and one HTTP 404 response were acquired and hashed. Twenty-five declared PDF text anchors were checked. The FY 2007 aggregate block and medium schedule rows were checked visually at 110 dpi. A text-layer screen of all **146** progress-report pages found zero matches for the two FAA IDs, the referral title phrase and the exact month-year phrase **December 2006**. The narrative aggregates, selected table rows and this literal screen cannot establish case membership, transmission or absence of an underlying index. The source ledger preserves the exact expressions and locators.
+
+- [ ] **PD04 / PD05.** Locate the **FY 2006–2007 Investigations Committee** schedule or working-group tracking table that identifies the six completed and two pending reviews, the EPA-to-DOT assignment and the operative guide version. Seek the revisions, approval and circulation records, and any predecessor-to-CIGIE record inventory.
+- [ ] **PD02–PD05.** Obtain the December 2006 report, EPA outgoing and DOT and DOJ receiving copies, complete scope and selection lists and case-keyed worksheets for **042R0122001**. The published 2012 comparator gives a retrieval pattern. It leaves 2006 scope and follow-up open. The corrected QFR and delivery, signed FAA action/no-action determination and recommendation-level implementation and closure remain separate open records. [DOJ recipient study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/1478d8d0b99f450ac6916433556de8735f4eb858/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-doj-peer-review-recipient-2026-11-10/README.md)
